===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# Closely wedged between two people.
#: {{co|en|to sit '''bodkin'''}}
#* {{RQ:Thackeray Vanity Fair|page=366|passage=He's too big to travel '''bodkin''' between you and me.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1904|author=Elizabeth von Arnim|title=The Adventures of Elizabeth in Rügen|publisher=MacMillan|year_published=1904
|passage=Either he must come between us and be what is known as bodkin, or some one must get out and walk; and the '''bodkin''' solution not commending itself to me it was plain that if some one walked it must be myself.}}

